                                "url": "https://www.advocate.com/politics/arlington-lgbtq-discrimination-protections-repeal",
                                "title": "Texas city could be first in nation to rescind LGBTQ+ anti-discrimination protections",
                                "domain": "advocate.com",
                                "pubDate": "2025-10-14T17:03:54+00:00",
                                "highlights": {
                                  "content": [
                                    "Related: Federal judge in Texas rules LGBTQ+ people can be discriminated against at work\nTrump officials threatened early last month to revoke $65 million in federal grant money from the city if it did not remove language related to diversity, equity and inclusion"
                                  ],
                                  "summary": [
                                    "This comes after the council temporarily suspended the clause due to threats from the Donald Trump administration. Both Arlington and Florida have voted to end their DEI programs and rewrite their ordinances to exclude phrases related to race and gender."
                                  ]
                                },
                                "sourceFavicon": "https://t1.gstatic.com/faviconV2?client=SOCIAL&type=FAVICON&fallback_opts=TYPE,SIZE,URL&url=https://advocate.com&size=32"
